{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"exact-identities-and-reductions","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765","passage_ref":"sha256:f7c2487ba172be55e583becc143742c2d34c576d0d1339fd730197a0c97bb374/papers/long.md/sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json/passages/exact-identities-and-reductions","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=exact-identities-and-reductions","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=exact-identities-and-reductions","span":{"end_byte":190836,"end_line":2055,"start_byte":157177,"start_line":1656},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.lem-denominator-survival&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.lem-denominator-survival&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.lem-denominator-survival&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.lem-denominator-survival&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&ref=sha256%3A264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c%2Fnodes%2Flong.lem-denominator-survival","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-denominator-survival"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-denominator-survival"],"id":"long.lem-denominator-survival","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.56 (A guaranteed divisor of a reduced denominator)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.56, p. 59, label lem:denominator-survival","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $a\\in\\mathbb Z$, $D\\in\\mathbb N_{>0}$ and $m,C,h\\in\\mathbb N$. Write $\\operatorname{den}(x)$ for the positive reduced denominator of a rational number $x$. If $m\\mid D$ and $\\gcd(m,|a|)=1$, then $m\\mid\\operatorname{den}(a/D)$. If $C\\mid D$ and $\\gcd(C,|a|)=1$, then\n$$\n\\frac{C}{\\gcd(C,h)}\\mid\\operatorname{den}(ha/D).\n$$\nThus scaling may remove part of the guaranteed divisor. Indeed, reduction divides $D$ by $\\gcd(D,|a|)$, so no prime power in $m$ can be lost. After scaling, a prime $p\\mid C$ can lose at most $v_p(h)$ powers from the guaranteed divisor. This is a lower bound on the reduced denominator, not an equality: for $D=12$, $C=6$, $a=1$, $h=2$, it guarantees the divisor $3$, while the reduced denominator is $6$. The lemma feeds Theorem 6.24 directly.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.lem-denominator-survival","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.lem-denominator-survival","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.lem-denominator-survival%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.RationalDenominatorSurvival.divisor_dvd_divInt_den%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.lem-denominator-survival%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.RationalDenominatorSurvival.divisor_dvd_divInt